# UI test: two type aliases that expand into each other (SC0524).
#
# Every name here resolves, so the resolver has nothing to say: the mistake is
# a property of the *expansion*. The check runs over the declarations rather
# than over the uses so that one cycle is one diagnostic — this file has no use
# of either alias and still reports, and a program with ten uses would report
# once as well.
#
# Both members are labelled, because neither declaration is the mistake on its
# own, and the note spells the chain out in expansion order — which the labels
# cannot, since the renderer sorts them by position.

type Name is Label

type Label is Name
